WEBVTT

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.990
You guys just keep on
eating and drinking here for free.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.560
I don't care if we're friends.
Any more and I'll make you pay up.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.940
Another round, please!

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.160
Judging by that look, he must've been here since the bar opened.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.330
But, man, you really are<i> amazing, Karube.</i>

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.400
We're the same age, but you already own a bar!

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.380
Even though he's only been to elementary school.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.510
Shut up.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:41.850
I've already decided I'm gonna buy a huge ranch in Australia and live my life there herding sheep.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.850
I'm saving up to make that dream a reality.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:50.330
So you couldn't bear the inferiority complex you have against your excellent younger brother,

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:53.770
and came running to my bar again?

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:57.490
Hey, if I actually knew what I was good at, I'd get my act together.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:04.200
Say, we get sent to an unknown place...

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.160
and the three of us have to participate in a survival game.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:09.920
If that happened, I'd definitely unlock my full potential!

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.670
Hey, Arisu, you forgot something.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.840
The place needs to be packed with babes!

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.140
That's all you ever think about.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:26.730
Was that... a dream?

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:33.850
Now that I think about it,

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.660
those seventeen years of my life
might've only been a dream.

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:42.580
The place I was living in until yesterday...

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:49.160
now feels like it was all just a part of a dream.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.760
Karube caught us some grub.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.430
Thanks, Karube-kun.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.680
It's so bland.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.600
Karube, don't you have any salt?

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.510
What? You get it from the ocean yourself.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:17.220
You didn't think about the taste or anything, did you?

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.740
You're slacking, Karube.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:23.450
Aw, man. You sure are useless.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.880
Those are some nice friends you've got there.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:26.950
That's right!

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:28.780
I know, right? We're the greatest friends a guy can have!

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.460
Don't get mad, man.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:31.510
I know, right? We're the greatest friends a guy can have!

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:39.260
You know, this is probably what it means to be alive.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.140
That's why...

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:47.140
we should participate in another game tonight.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.970
Wait, Karube! We're still safe for three more days.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:56.110
He's right! Besides, Chouta-kun is injured.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.110
Of course, Chouta will sit this one out.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.440
Now you're really not making any sense!

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:01.360
Arisu.

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:05.800
You feel relieved that you're still alive, right?

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.370
To me, that's dangerous.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:15.260
In order to fully realize the strengths
we displayed during yesterday's game,

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:18.340
we need to get accustomed to the
feeling of putting our lives on the line.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:24.000
That's why, before we start feeling relaxed,
we should participate in another game tonight.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.870
What we need is the iron hearts of soldiers on the line of duty.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.120
Right now, we must sharpen our fangs.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.690
Much sharper!

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.780
We can't survive unless we do that.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:36.830
I won't be there to protect you guys all the time.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.900
I-I know what you're trying to say...

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:46.030
That means all of your visas will be extended, right?

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:52.540
So when my visa expires two days from now,
will you guys participate in a game with me?

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.380
What are you talking about, Chouta?
Of course we'll—

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.800
I'll stay behind with Chouta-kun.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:02.130
I won't let you feel anxious all by yourself.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.980
When it comes down to it, I'll be going with you.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:10.930
I'm the only one who's useless.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:14.060
I'm just dead weight to you guys.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:27.740
You're not dead weight, Chouta!

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:31.830
The fish you caught got me all energized.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:35.790
So don't worry about a thing.
Just focus on getting better.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.630
You're all fired up for once.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:44.040
Comparing yourself to others...
Being compared to others...

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.140
I'm done moping around.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:50.300
Let's go there once more...

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:54.850
to figure out who I really am, and what I'm capable of.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:00.720
Let's go.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:01.650
Yeah.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:10.530
I'll catch so many fish for you tomorrow that you won't be able to finish them all.

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:41.370
What the hell is that?

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:42.280
It's shining.

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:44.620
You go touch it!

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:45.110
No way!

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:46.360
Attention, everyone.
No way!

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:50.460
It is now six o'clock.
It's time for the game to commence.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:55.690
A terrifying killer is lurking in the shadows, so please be careful on your way home.

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:59.040
A killer?

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:03.800
The game you all will be playing is tag.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:06.740
You will be running around in this complex.
We're gonna play tag!

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:09.170
We're not kids, you know?

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:10.750
Arisu.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:14.850
I know. They're like us from yesterday.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:19.040
The game's difficulty level is five of spades.
They don't know that this is reality.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.310
Anything we say now is pointless.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:25.350
Oh, damn. We got spades of all the suits.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:26.550
What's wrong with spades?

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.700
Games of spades are all about physical effort.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.410
I'm not good at those.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:34.560
The time limit is thirty minutes.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.370
The person who's <i>it</i> will start hunting in five minutes.

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:42.630
In this whole complex, there's one room that's not locked.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:46.340
That's the home base of the person who's <i>it</i>.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:52.390
If you reach the home base within
the time limit, the game will be cleared.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.150
Let's get moving too.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:55.330
Yeah.

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:57.970
I'll stick with you two.

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:04.820
The game is over when time runs out,
or when all of the players have been killed.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:09.350
When the time limit is up,
this building will be blown up.

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:13.740
Furthermore, the building is surrounded by land mines,

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.580
so please make sure you do not go outside.

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:22.760
In this game, choosing your first spot is the most important.

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:26.620
To move within the building, there are stairs in the center,

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:29.840
the southern wing,

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:33.510
and the western wing.

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.490
There's also an elevator in the center.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.880
From here, we can keep watch in all three directions.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.880
If you sense the guy who's <i>it</i>, tell us right away.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:44.400
Got it.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.440
Is this really the best move?

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:57.070
Think! Observation and analysis is what you're good at.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:07:59.950
Just as I thought.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:05.290
The most important point in this game is, without a doubt, choosing your first spot.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:11.800
When you don't know where the killer will come from, the best option is to go to the top floor.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.950
From here, I can get a grasp of most of the situation.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:19.300
The first victim who'll provide important information...

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.520
will be from somewhere around there.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.440
That's the sound of a door!

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:38.750
It must be the killer!

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:39.990
Where'd it come from?

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.130
I couldn't tell because of the echo!

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:47.790
I couldn't see a door opening from here.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:49.330
Which means...

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:54.340
The killer's home base must be
somewhere in the southern wing, or...

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:59.600
Well, it'd be boring if it were that easy to figure out.

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:07.060
It doesn't matter how many people he's killed; he's not as smart as me.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.970
Wh-What was <i>that</i> sound just now?!

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.780
It came from an upper floor!

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.690
It was my first time hearing a real machine gun.

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:32.920
I felt the same as a stray cat being scared off by firecracker.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:38.510
My first time seeing a murder was like seeing a jar of jam

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.800
having its contents emptied and fulfilling its role.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:05.280
Wh-Wh-What the hell is that?!

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:07.000
Hell if I know! Fuck!

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:10.500
Karube, this way!

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:12.080
You too! Hurry!

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:13.910
N-No way!

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:16.480
Arisu, we should hurry up and run!

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:17.200
Come this way!

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.220
Trust me and just hold your breath.

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:42.450
I see.

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:45.860
Against a machine gun, no matter what floor you go down to,

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:49.540
you'll be shot to death in the hallway
before you even reach the center staircase.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:54.280
But in this situation, it's only natural that one would go down as many floors as possible.

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:56.200
The killer must've thought of that too.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:11:00.800
If you were gonna gamble anyway,
the third floor is the best bet.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.760
The participants this time are at a pretty high level.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.230
I guess...

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:13.060
I'm not really cut out for spades.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.900
Another gunfire...

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:24.120
They're dead. I just saw people shot to death before my very eyes.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:29.130
We're still alive, aren't we? Right?!

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:32.480
Yeah. We're still alive.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:33.330
Arisu!

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.090
The killer was dragging his foot.

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:39.600
Even with the range he gets from the machine gun,
we can move faster than him.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:43.340
We can't clear this game by just running away.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:47.980
Now that the killer is away from us,
it's our best chance to find the home base!

00:11:50.030 --> 00:11:54.360
Hey! Everyone! Can you hear me?!

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:58.130
The killer is a huge guy wearing a horse mask!

00:11:58.130 --> 00:12:02.130
We should all yell out and tell each other the killer's location!

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:06.030
Then those who are out of danger can look for the home base freely!

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:09.080
We're all gonna make it out alive!

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:12.880
He's fired up. And he's also sharp.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:15.540
But will things actually work that easily?

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:21.170
"There are a lot of other people here, so is there a need to put myself at risk by looking for the home base?"

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:26.430
"Wouldn't yelling out mean giving away my position to the killer?"

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:31.680
"In the first place, can I even trust the
information from complete strangers?"

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:34.620
Whether it be on the other side of the earth, or right in front of their eyes,

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:38.730
these guys don't care how many people die as long as they're safe.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.660
That's just human nature.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:42.860
The killer is on the sixth floor's southern hallway!

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:45.070
Those who are nearby, get away immediately!

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:50.370
I stand corrected.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:55.290
This way is not good!

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.000
The killer is just right around the corner!

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:57.960
What?

00:12:58.860 --> 00:12:59.960
I'm sorry.

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:02.050
I couldn't help you.

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:12.260
Did you see that just now?

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:13.890
Does she do gymnastics or something?

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:16.850
A climber?

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:24.740
To hell with this. No way am I getting shot to death.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:28.820
I'm getting out...
I'm getting out of here!

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:31.550
What was that?!

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:35.040
Someone tried to leave the building.

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:42.630
Hey, you there.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:47.550
You have great form. You did some combat sports?

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:49.760
Wrestling.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:54.710
In close combat, would you be able to break the killer's neck?

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:56.310
Damn it!

00:13:57.640 --> 00:13:59.170
Not on this floor either!

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:00.870
This complex is too big.

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:04.650
We'll run out of time if we check all the doors one by one.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.070
We've already used up ten minutes.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:09.130
What are the others doing?

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:12.030
It's a good thing that we haven't heard any gunshots though.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:14.660
Anyway, we've got no choice but to keep searching for the home base!

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:15.700
Let's go, Arisu!

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:18.250
A-Already?

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:22.250
If I knew this would happen,
I would've joined some sports team.

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:25.930
I've always been like that.

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:31.130
I was never really passionate about studying or sports.

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:37.390
I was one of those people who didn't prepare for his future.

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:41.020
I really hate myself.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:43.320
Arisu, hurry up!

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:47.780
Arisu!

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.460
Did he see me?

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:55.950
No, he was aiming at Karube.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:57.600
Or was<i> he?</i>

00:14:57.600 --> 00:14:58.720
Scratch that thought.

00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:02.880
Either way, I need to believe that he didn't see me,

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.820
and just wait for him to pass by.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:08.590
Don't breathe. I should also stop the beating of my—

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:11.050
L-Like hell I can do that!

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:14.620
No good. My body won't stop shaking.

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:17.020
I'm scared...
I'm very scared!

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:19.480
I'm so fucking scared!

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:22.060
He'll definitely notice me!

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.020
It's over!

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:27.500
He'll notice me! This time, I might really...

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:29.700
die.

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:34.660
You really are a son I can take pride in.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:37.410
Thank you very much, Dad.

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:42.170
Why? Why am I remembering this now?

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:46.000
Damn it! It's my fault!

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:48.920
I shouldn't have left him alone!

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.360
Damn it all!

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:53.680
What the?

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:55.330
That's not the killer.

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:00.770
What are you guys doing?

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:06.230
We're switching places with the killer. This time, <i>we're</i> gonna hunt him.

00:16:08.350 --> 00:16:10.200
I see. It's the same situation.

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:14.450
I didn't exist in that household.

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:29.840
In life, you never know what might come in handy.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:31.820
I get it now.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:35.800
Whether it's an inferiority complex or whatever, I just need to turn it into my own weapon.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:39.310
I know what I need in order to survive!

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:42.480
Hey, dumbass!

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:45.770
Are you gonna kill me or what?

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:48.730
I didn't hear any gunfire back then.

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:51.190
Arisu, please be alive!

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:02.910
Now!

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:08.480
Break his neck!

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:12.170
Don't worry. He'll drop dead in a few seconds.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.680
Of course he does.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.730
Why did I assume

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:26.790
he was only carrying one gun?

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:29.020
Damn it!

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:34.110
The gunfires went on for a long time...

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:39.070
Someone must be giving it their all.
They're idiots if they think they can change the rules.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:42.580
Did that gunfire come from around the center?

00:17:45.180 --> 00:17:45.830
Karube!

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:57.380
Arisu... So you really are still alive!

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.690
You had me so worried...

00:17:59.690 --> 00:18:01.850
Damn it.

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:10.980
Is he heading this way?

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:14.070
Those are...

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.240
Put yourself in the killer's shoes...

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:21.730
Why is he heading this way?
Why did he shoot at me<i>?</i>

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:23.510
Is it because he heard me?

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:24.370
Probably not.

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:29.210
Those bullet holes must be from his first shot.

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:33.620
There's only a slim chance that you'll
hit someone running from across the balcony.

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:35.600
If he didn't mean to kill them...

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:37.420
A warning shot?

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:40.640
All right!

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:46.560
That's right. If I put myself in the killer's shoes, there's no need to hunt the players.

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:49.220
He just needs to protect the home base!

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:53.400
But that's the same as telling us where the home base is.

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:55.400
It'll be bad for him if we concentrate our attack.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:58.400
To hide that fact, we play a game of tag!

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:00.410
There's only one minute left.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:03.870
If I were it<i>, I would stand
guard in front of the home base now.</i>

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:13.880
It seems he finally noticed. They'll need a hand.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:15.460
I guess it's time to move.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.880
Everyone! The home base is over here!

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:25.560
Arisu!

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:43.220
There. I bought you some time.

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.490
It's no good, Karube!

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:47.310
One person can't clear this game!

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:50.500
You have to press two buttons at the same time!

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:54.040
What?!

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.090
Oh, shit!

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:58.550
Somebody, please come.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.510
Somebody!

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:06.680
You called?

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:28.290
You got us all worked up, damn it.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:32.000
It was a bit close this time.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:36.460
I'm alive... I'm still alive!

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:33.620
<b>If you say any more than that,
we'll no longer be friends.</b>

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:39.670
<b>Anyway, to save myself,
three people will have to die!</b>

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:46.020
Next time on <i>Alice in Borderland</i>:

00:22:46.020 --> 00:22:46.720
<b>I'm dropping out of this "game."</b>

00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:48.620
Next time on <i>Alice in Borderland</i>:

00:22:49.350 --> 00:22:52.750
Game Three: the Seven of Hearts.
